From 6ee47e7502f7bdec49c004f65e40d2dc2776fccd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:47:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(android): append --inline-3d-occlusion by default, as
 Windows does

Patch 0065 put the default-append of --inline-3d-occlusion inside
`#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)`, and no Android patch (0083-0102) ever added the
matching arm -- patch 0096's own comment says so in as many words ("inline-3D
is not yet on by default on Android (the block above is IS_WIN-only)").

So on Android the switch was never on unless a human wrote it into
/data/local/tmp/chrome-command-line by hand, and with it off
inline3d_occlusion_enabled_ is false in BOTH readers: DirectRenderer on the GPU
compositor thread, which builds the plane split, and SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu
on the GPU main thread, which composites the over-plane. The whole Phase-2
2D-over-3D path was therefore dead code on the device, and every 2D element
painted above an inline-3D tile was buried by the tile -- the reported defect.

Mirror the IS_WIN logic rather than invent new logic. Same precedence:
--disable-inline-3d-occlusion wins and removes the switch, an explicit
--inline-3d-occlusion is left exactly as given, otherwise the default is
appended. ChromeContentBrowserClient::AppendExtraCommandLineSwitches already
forwards whatever survives to the GPU and renderer processes, so it needs no
change.

Scoped to the same `enable-inline-3d` guard as the AndroidSurfaceControl
override it sits beside, deliberately: inline-3D itself is still opt-in on
Android (it arrives through the command-line file, which Android parses into
base::CommandLine before ContentMain runs). Turning the whole feature on by
default is a different change than fixing its occlusion sub-switch, and is not
made here.
---
 chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc b/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
index 4481cd6028f2e..d21a1097683ee 100644
--- a/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
@@ -1176,6 +1176,35 @@ std::optional<int> ChromeMainDelegate::BasicStartupComplete() {
       disabled += "AndroidSurfaceControl";
       mutable_command_line->AppendSwitchASCII("disable-features", disabled);
     }
+    // Phase-2 plane split / occlusion, mirrored from the IS_WIN block above.
+    //
+    // THE BUG THIS FIXES: patch 0065 put the default-append of
+    // --inline-3d-occlusion inside `#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)`, and no Android
+    // patch ever added the matching arm — patch 0096's own comment says so in
+    // as many words. So on Android inline3d_occlusion_enabled_ was false in
+    // BOTH readers (DirectRenderer on the GPU compositor thread, which builds
+    // the split, and SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu on the GPU main thread, which
+    // composites the over-plane), the whole Phase-2 path was dead, and 2D
+    // content over a woven tile was buried by the tile. That is the
+    // device-visible "the overlay disappears and the tile shows instead".
+    //
+    // Same precedence as Windows, deliberately not reinvented:
+    // --disable-inline-3d-occlusion wins and removes the switch; an explicit
+    // --inline-3d-occlusion is left exactly as the user gave it; otherwise the
+    // default is appended. Scoped to the same `enable-inline-3d` guard as the
+    // SurfaceControl override above rather than made unconditional, because
+    // inline-3D itself is still opt-in on Android (it arrives via
+    // /data/local/tmp/chrome-command-line, parsed into base::CommandLine
+    // before ContentMain runs) — turning the whole feature on by default here
+    // would be a different change than fixing its occlusion sub-switch.
+    //
+    // ChromeContentBrowserClient::AppendExtraCommandLineSwitches forwards
+    // whatever survives to the GPU and renderer processes; it needs no change.
+    if (mutable_command_line->HasSwitch("disable-inline-3d-occlusion")) {
+      mutable_command_line->RemoveSwitch("inline-3d-occlusion");
+    } else if (!mutable_command_line->HasSwitch("inline-3d-occlusion")) {
+      mutable_command_line->AppendSwitch("inline-3d-occlusion");
+    }
   }
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
 
